div.div:

      5 
      تزعّم  i. q. تَكَذَّبَ [q. v.]: (S, K:) [it seems
here to mean He spoke falsely; and to be trans.;
for] a poet says,
“أَيُّهَا الزَّاعِمُ مَا تَزَعَّمَا

”
[app. meaning O thou asserter of that which thou
hast spoken falsely]. (TA. [This hemistich is
there cited as an ex. of تزعّم as expl. in the K;
and I find no other explanation of this verb.])
